---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AtlasBackdrop from '../../components/AtlasBackdrop';
import Cartouche from '../../components/Cartouche.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case Study: Infrastructure Platform Migration"
  description="How Infrastructure as Code and container orchestration eliminated snowflake servers and reduced deployment lead time from days to minutes across 14 production services."
>
  <AtlasBackdrop client:only="react" />

  <main class="case-study-page">

    <!-- ── Breadcrumb & header ─────────────────────────────────── -->
    <header class="cs-header">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href={base + '/'}>Atlas</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> › </span>
        <a href={base + '/infra'}>Infrastructure</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> › </span>
        <span>Case Study</span>
      </div>

      <Cartouche label="Case study · Plate v-A · Infrastructure Architecture">
        <div class="cs-title-block">
          <p class="cs-catalogue">Study ref. INFRA-01</p>
          <h1 class="cs-title">Infrastructure Platform Migration</h1>
          <p class="cs-subtitle">Infrastructure as Code &amp; Container Orchestration at Scale</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-meta-row">
          <div class="cs-meta-item">
            <span class="meta-label">Context</span>
            <span class="meta-value">E-commerce platform, 14 production services</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-meta-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="cs-meta-item">
            <span class="meta-label">Scale</span>
            <span class="meta-value">~3M daily active users, peak 8× baseline</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-meta-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="cs-meta-item">
            <span class="meta-label">Duration</span>
            <span class="meta-value">16 weeks (rolling cutover)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-meta-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="cs-meta-item">
            <span class="meta-label">Role</span>
            <span class="meta-value">Lead Solution Architect</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Cartouche>
    </header>

    <!-- ── Context ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="cs-section">
      <Cartouche label="I — Context &amp; Problem Statement">
        <div class="prose-grid">
          <div class="prose-main">
            <h2 class="section-heading">The Situation</h2>
            <p>
              A mid-size e-commerce platform had grown from a single on-premises host into
              a sprawl of fourteen virtual machines across two cloud providers. Each server
              had been provisioned manually, patched ad hoc, and configured over time through
              SSH sessions that left no audit trail. No two hosts were identical. The
              deployment process was a bespoke shell script — different for every service —
              that a single senior engineer maintained and understood.
            </p>
            <p>
              The consequence was chronic: a production incident in Q4 peak season revealed
              that three services were running different versions of the same shared library.
              Recovery required four hours of manual reconciliation. Horizontal scaling
              during peak load was impossible because new instances would diverge from
              production state within hours. The platform was entirely dependent on one
              person's institutional knowledge to recover from failure.
            </p>

            <h2 class="section-heading">Constraints</h2>
            <ul class="prose-list">
              <li>Zero-downtime migration — e-commerce cannot afford planned outages</li>
              <li>Multi-cloud: AWS for compute, GCP for data services — must work across both</li>
              <li>Team of six: one infrastructure specialist, five application engineers</li>
              <li>No Kubernetes experience on the team — tooling choice must be learnable</li>
              <li>Peak season (Q4) in 20 weeks — full migration must complete before then</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <aside class="prose-sidebar">
            <Cartouche label="Patterns applied">
              <ul class="sidebar-list">
                <li>
                  <span class="pattern-bullet" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>
                  <a href={base + '/infra#infrastructure-as-code'} class="pattern-link">
                    Infrastructure as Code
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="pattern-bullet" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>
                  <a href={base + '/infra#docker-port-mapping'} class="pattern-link">
                    Container Isolation
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="pattern-bullet" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>
                  <a href={base + '/infra#multi-database-orchestration'} class="pattern-link">
                    Multi-Database Orchestration
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="pattern-bullet" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>
                  <a href={base + '/anti-patterns#snowflake-server'} class="pattern-link">
                    Anti: Snowflake Server
                  </a>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </Cartouche>

            <Cartouche label="Outcome metrics">
              <ul class="sidebar-metrics">
                <li>
                  <span class="metric-num">96%</span>
                  <span class="metric-label">reduction in deployment lead time</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="metric-num">0</span>
                  <span class="metric-label">snowflake servers remaining</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="metric-num">4 min</span>
                  <span class="metric-label">mean recovery time (down from 4 hrs)</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="metric-num">8×</span>
                  <span class="metric-label">peak traffic handled without manual scaling</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </Cartouche>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </Cartouche>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Architecture diagram ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="cs-section">
      <Cartouche label="II — Architecture Diagram · Before &amp; After">
        <div class="diagram-header">
          <h2 class="section-heading">Platform Evolution</h2>
          <p class="diagram-caption">
            Left: original state — heterogeneous VMs, no declared configuration, manual
            deployments. Right: target state — immutable images built from source, Terraform
            managing all cloud resources, Kubernetes orchestrating workloads declaratively.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-container">
          <!-- ── Before ───────────────── -->
          <figure class="diagram-figure">
            <figcaption class="diagram-label">Before — Snowflake VM Estate</figcaption>
            <svg
              class="arch-diagram"
              viewBox="0 0 340 380"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Before: three unique VMs each manually configured, pointed to shared database, deployed via SSH"
            >
              <rect width="340" height="380" fill="rgba(10,14,26,0.0)" />

              <!-- Outer boundary: manual estate -->
              <rect x="20" y="20" width="300" height="280" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.02)" stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.18)" stroke-width="0.5"
                stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
              <text x="170" y="38" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="2"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.35)">MANUAL VM ESTATE</text>

              <!-- VM A (unique) -->
              <rect x="30" y="50" width="80" height="48" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.1)" stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="70" y="70" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.9)">VM-A</text>
              <text x="70" y="83" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.5)">node 14.8 · custom</text>
              <text x="70" y="93" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)">nginx 1.18</text>

              <!-- VM B (different) -->
              <rect x="130" y="50" width="80" height="48" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.1)" stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="70" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.9)">VM-B</text>
              <text x="170" y="83" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.5)">node 16.2 · patched</text>
              <text x="170" y="93" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)">nginx 1.22</text>

              <!-- VM C (different again) -->
              <rect x="230" y="50" width="80" height="48" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.1)" stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="270" y="70" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.9)">VM-C</text>
              <text x="270" y="83" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.5)">node 14.15 · drift</text>
              <text x="270" y="93" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)">apache 2.4</text>

              <!-- SSH deploy lines -->
              <text x="170" y="118" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="2"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.5)">↓ SSH DEPLOY (MANUAL) ↓</text>

              <!-- Shared DB -->
              <rect x="95" y="132" width="150" height="44" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(90,79,51,0.2)" stroke="rgba(212,177,94,0.25)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="152" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.6)">SHARED DATABASE</text>
              <text x="170" y="167" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.35)">single host, no replica</text>

              <!-- Lines from VMs to DB -->
              <line x1="70" y1="98" x2="120" y2="132"
                stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.3)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <line x1="170" y1="98" x2="170" y2="132"
                stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.3)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <line x1="270" y1="98" x2="220" y2="132"
                stroke="rgba(196,106,85,0.3)" stroke-width="0.5" />

              <!-- Problem annotation -->
              <text x="170" y="210" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.7)">NO TWO VMs IDENTICAL</text>
              <text x="170" y="228" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.5)">UNDOCUMENTED CONFIGURATION</text>
              <text x="170" y="246" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.4)">SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE</text>

              <defs>
                <marker id="arrowRed" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="rgba(196,106,85,0.6)" />
                </marker>
              </defs>
            </svg>
          </figure>

          <!-- ── Divider ──────────────── -->
          <div class="diagram-divider" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="divider-glyph">→</span>
          </div>

          <!-- ── After ────────────────── -->
          <figure class="diagram-figure">
            <figcaption class="diagram-label">After — Declarative Platform</figcaption>
            <svg
              class="arch-diagram"
              viewBox="0 0 340 380"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              role="img"
              aria-label="After: Terraform declares cloud resources, CI builds immutable images, Kubernetes runs identical pods from those images"
            >
              <rect width="340" height="380" fill="rgba(10,14,26,0.0)" />

              <!-- Terraform layer -->
              <rect x="20" y="20" width="300" height="44" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.08)" stroke="rgba(200,164,212,0.35)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="38" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="2"
                fill="#c8a4d4">TERRAFORM</text>
              <text x="170" y="54" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.5)">cloud resources declared in source</text>

              <!-- Arrow down -->
              <line x1="170" y1="64" x2="170" y2="84"
                stroke="rgba(200,164,212,0.4)" stroke-width="0.5" marker-end="url(#arrowPurple)" />

              <!-- CI / image build -->
              <rect x="90" y="84" width="160" height="44" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(158,196,138,0.08)" stroke="rgba(158,196,138,0.35)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="104" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="2"
                fill="#9ec48a">CI PIPELINE</text>
              <text x="170" y="118" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(158,196,138,0.5)">immutable image build + push</text>

              <!-- Arrow down -->
              <line x1="170" y1="128" x2="170" y2="148"
                stroke="rgba(158,196,138,0.4)" stroke-width="0.5" marker-end="url(#arrowGreen2)" />

              <!-- Kubernetes cluster -->
              <rect x="20" y="148" width="300" height="120" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.04)" stroke="rgba(212,177,94,0.3)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="164" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" letter-spacing="2"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.6)">KUBERNETES CLUSTER</text>

              <!-- Pod A -->
              <rect x="34" y="172" width="72" height="36" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.1)" stroke="rgba(200,164,212,0.35)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="70" y="188" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="#c8a4d4">POD</text>
              <text x="70" y="201" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="6" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.5)">image:v2.4.1</text>

              <!-- Pod B -->
              <rect x="134" y="172" width="72" height="36" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.1)" stroke="rgba(200,164,212,0.35)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="188" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="#c8a4d4">POD</text>
              <text x="170" y="201" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="6" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.5)">image:v2.4.1</text>

              <!-- Pod C -->
              <rect x="234" y="172" width="72" height="36" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.1)" stroke="rgba(200,164,212,0.35)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="270" y="188" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="#c8a4d4">POD</text>
              <text x="270" y="201" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="6" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.5)">image:v2.4.1</text>

              <!-- Identical label -->
              <text x="170" y="232" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="2"
                fill="rgba(158,196,138,0.6)">IDENTICAL · IMMUTABLE · REPRODUCIBLE</text>

              <!-- Arrow to DB -->
              <line x1="170" y1="268" x2="170" y2="290"
                stroke="rgba(212,177,94,0.4)" stroke-width="0.5" marker-end="url(#arrowGold2)" />

              <!-- Managed DB -->
              <rect x="95" y="290" width="150" height="44" rx="0"
                fill="rgba(90,79,51,0.2)" stroke="rgba(212,177,94,0.35)" stroke-width="0.5" />
              <text x="170" y="310" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="1.5"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.7)">MANAGED DB</text>
              <text x="170" y="325" text-anchor="middle"
                font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" letter-spacing="1"
                fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.4)">RDS · declared in Terraform</text>

              <defs>
                <marker id="arrowPurple" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="rgba(200,164,212,0.6)" />
                </marker>
                <marker id="arrowGreen2" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="rgba(158,196,138,0.6)" />
                </marker>
                <marker id="arrowGold2" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="rgba(212,177,94,0.6)" />
                </marker>
              </defs>
            </svg>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p class="diagram-note">
          The critical shift: infrastructure state lives in version control, not on
          individual hosts. Every pod runs from the same immutable image. Desired state
          is declared once; the platform converges to it — continuously.
        </p>
      </Cartouche>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Approach ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="cs-section">
      <Cartouche label="III — Approach &amp; Key Decisions">
        <div class="approach-grid">
          <div class="approach-col">
            <h2 class="section-heading">Phase 1: Terraform Foundation (Weeks 1–4)</h2>
            <p>
              Before touching a single container, all existing cloud resources were imported
              into Terraform state. This exposed configuration drift immediately — eighteen
              security group rules that existed in production but not in any documentation.
              The import process itself served as a configuration audit.
            </p>
            <p>
              Every subsequent cloud resource change was gated behind a <code>terraform plan</code>
              review in CI. No engineer could modify a security group, subnet, or IAM role
              outside source control. Drift detection ran nightly and opened a ticket on
              any discrepancy.
            </p>

            <h2 class="section-heading">Phase 2: Containerisation (Weeks 5–10)</h2>
            <p>
              Services were containerised in order of risk: stateless services first,
              stateful workers last. Each Dockerfile was written to produce deterministic
              images — pinned base images, no package manager operations at runtime,
              non-root user, read-only filesystem where possible.
            </p>
            <p>
              A key decision was to avoid custom Helm charts initially. Plain Kubernetes
              manifests in a <code>k8s/</code> directory per service kept the learning
              curve manageable. Complexity was deferred until the team had operational
              experience with the platform.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="approach-col">
            <h2 class="section-heading">Phase 3: Progressive Traffic Cutover (Weeks 11–16)</h2>
            <p>
              Traffic was shifted to Kubernetes pods using weighted DNS — 5% initially,
              increasing to 100% over four weeks per service. Rollback required only a
              DNS weight change, executable in under 90 seconds. No service required
              a maintenance window.
            </p>
            <p>
              Kubernetes liveness and readiness probes replaced the previous monitoring
              approach, which had been manual health checks every 15 minutes. The platform
              now self-healed: a crashed pod was replaced within 30 seconds, automatically,
              without paging anyone.
            </p>

            <h2 class="section-heading">Horizontal Pod Autoscaling</h2>
            <p>
              HPA was configured for each stateless service with CPU-based scaling and a
              minimum replica count of 2. Q4 peak — the original forcing function for
              this project — arrived eight weeks after the migration completed.
              Traffic peaked at 8× baseline. The platform scaled automatically; no engineer
              intervention was required. The incident that had taken four hours to resolve
              the prior year did not recur.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Cartouche>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Results ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="cs-section">
      <Cartouche label="IV — Results &amp; Reflection">
        <div class="results-grid">
          <div class="result-card">
            <span class="result-num">96%</span>
            <p class="result-label">Deployment lead time reduction</p>
            <p class="result-detail">Days of manual coordination → 4-minute CI pipeline</p>
          </div>
          <div class="result-card">
            <span class="result-num">0</span>
            <p class="result-label">Snowflake servers remaining</p>
            <p class="result-detail">All 14 services running from declared, versioned configuration</p>
          </div>
          <div class="result-card">
            <span class="result-num">4 min</span>
            <p class="result-label">Mean time to recovery</p>
            <p class="result-detail">Down from 4 hours — Kubernetes self-heals without manual intervention</p>
          </div>
          <div class="result-card">
            <span class="result-num">8×</span>
            <p class="result-label">Peak traffic handled</p>
            <p class="result-detail">HPA scaled automatically through Q4 — no incidents, no pages</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="reflection">
          <h2 class="section-heading">What I Would Do Differently</h2>
          <p>
            The Terraform import phase surfaced 18 undocumented security group rules —
            each required a decision about whether it was intentional or legacy drift.
            That review consumed two full weeks that were not in the original estimate.
            In future migrations I would schedule a dedicated configuration audit sprint
            before committing to an IaC import timeline.
          </p>
          <p>
            Plain Kubernetes manifests worked well for the initial migration but became
            difficult to maintain across 14 services as each accumulated environment-specific
            patches. Adopting Kustomize overlays at week 10 — rather than week 14 —
            would have avoided the duplication that accumulated in the final push.
            The lesson: keep the tooling simple to start, but identify the abstraction
            threshold before you hit it, not after.
          </p>
          <p>
            The most underestimated factor was cultural: engineers accustomed to SSH
            access felt a loss of control when direct host modification was prohibited.
            Investing in runbook documentation and a clear escalation path for "I need
            to change something and CI is broken" would have reduced friction in the
            first month of the new workflow.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Cartouche>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Navigation ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="cs-footer">
      <div class="footer-nav">
        <a href={base + '/infra'} class="nav-link">← Infrastructure Domain</a>
        <a href={base + '/case-studies/backend-api-redesign'} class="nav-link">
          Case Study: Backend API Redesign →
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="footer-coord">Plate v-A · Case Study INFRA-01 · RA +120° Dec −560°</p>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .case-study-page {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 80px 32px 120px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 48px;
  }

  /* ── Breadcrumb ── */
  .breadcrumb {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
